cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "multipoles: Multipole expansions of electrostatic and gravitational potentials in Python"
abstract: >-
  multipoles computes the multipole expansion of point charges or of a charge density on a grid,
  and evaluates the potential, its field and its Hessian with a rigorous error bound. It supports
  exterior and interior expansions, unevenly spaced grids, electrostatics and gravity.
authors:
  - family-names: Baer
    given-names: Matthias
version: 0.6.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/maroba/multipoles"
url: "https://maroba.github.io/multipoles/"
keywords:
  - multipole expansion
  - Poisson equation
  - electrostatics
  - gravity
  - physics
  - Python
